4. The KAG Recurse & RLVR Feedback Cycle
The interaction dynamics between working context, episodic telemetry, and procedural refinement operate in a closed recursive loop:
[ Attempt Start ] ──> Working Memory (Context Window loads task + Tier 3 context)
       │
       ├───> Invokes Procedural Layer (Tier 4: Skill definitions & tool execution)
       │
       ├───> Produces Intermediate Output (Attempt #N: code execution, validation step)
       │
       ├───> Streams Event to Episodic Log (Tier 5: Prompt -> Code -> Error/Success)
       │
       ▼
[ Verifier Evaluation ]
       │
       ├─── If FAILED (-1.0 Reward):
       │      └── Trigger Recursive Backtracking (load error trace into Context Window, retry)
       │
       └─── If SUCCEEDED (+1.0 Reward):
              └── Commit trajectory to Episodic Vector DB
              └── Distill learned pattern into Tier 2 (Wiki) and Tier 4 (Procedural Prompts)

1. Working Memory (Context Window): Loads immediate system instructions, active variables, and dynamic tokens retrieved from Tier 3 (/recall_cache/).
2. Procedural Action (Tier 4): The model applies algorithmic habits and tool-calling scripts from /skills/ to evaluate code, query resources, or manipulate data.
3. Episodic Capture (Tier 5): The raw input-output sequence of Attempt #42 is written to /episodic_logs/ as an immutable run trace (Prompt \to Action \to Environment Feedback \to Verifier Score).
4. Reinforcement Learning via Verifiable Rewards (RLVR): The verifier inspects the episodic record. Negative rewards trigger automated backtracking in working memory. Consistently successful runs are extracted into permanent procedural skills (Tier 4) or base policy weight updates.
